hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16145","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi. My father said, and Ibn Jafar said: From Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best houses of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah, and in all the houses of the Ansar is good. So Sad ibn Ubadah said: I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has but preferred over us. So it was said: He has preferred you over many."
"16146","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah. Then he said: And in all the houses of the Ansar is good."
"16147","He said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The best houses of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah. Then he said: And in all the houses of the Ansar is good. So Sad ibn Ubadah said: He made us fourth of four. Saddle for me my donkey. His nephew said: Do you want to retort upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It suffices you to be fourth of four."
"16148","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah, and in all the Ansar is good."
"16149","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, that he heard Abu Usayd, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best dwellings of the Ansar. And he mentioned the hadith."
"16150","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, he said: Ata, a man who was at the coast, narrated to me, from Abu Usayd or Abu Usayd ibn Thabit, Sufyan doubted, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat oil and anoint with oil, for it is from a blessed tree."
"16151","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Ata al-Shami, from Abu Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat oil and anoint with it, for it is from a blessed tree."
"16152","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that Abu Usayd used to say: I obtained on the day of Badr the sword of Ibn Abid al-Marzuban. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that they return what was in their hands, I came with it until I cast it into the spoils. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not withhold anything he was asked. He said: Al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam al-Makhzumi recognized it, and asked it of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave it to him."
"16153","It was read to Yaqub in the maghazi of his father, or hearing. Ibn Ishaq said, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, he said: Some of Banu Saidah narrated to me, from Abu Usayd Malik ibn Rabiah, he said: I obtained the sword of Banu Abid al-Makhzumis, al-Marzuban, on the day of Badr. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people to render what was in their hands of spoils, I came with it until I cast it into the spoils. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not withhold anything he was asked. Al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam recognized it, and asked it of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave it to him."
"16154","He said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Suwayd al-Ansari, he said: I heard Abu Humayd and Abu Usayd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him say: O Allah, open for us the doors of Thy mercy. And when he goes out, let him say: O Allah, I ask Thee of Thy bounty."
"16155","He said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Suwayd, from Abu Humayd and from Abu Usayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear a hadith from me your hearts recognize and your hairs and skins soften to it, and you see it near to you, then I am most worthy of it. And when you hear a hadith from me your hearts deny and your hairs and skins shrink from it, and you see it far from you, then I am furthest of you from it."
"16156","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, he said: Usayd ibn Ali narrated to me, from his father Ali ibn Ubayd, from Abu Usayd, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was a Badri, and he was their freedman. He said: Abu Usayd said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Ansar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, does there remain upon me of dutifulness to my parents anything after their death I do dutifulness to them with? He said: Yes, four traits: prayer over them, and seeking forgiveness for them, and carrying out their covenant, and honoring their friend, and joining the kinship which is kinship for you only through them. So it is what remains upon you of their dutifulness after their death."
"16157","He said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil informed us, from Abbas ibn Sahl, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, he said: When we met us and the people on the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us that day: When they overwhelm you, meaning cover you, shoot them with arrows. And I think he said: And spare your arrows."
"16158","He said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, and Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us, and companions with him, so we went out with him until we set out to a garden called al-Shawt, until we reached two walls of it, and we sat between them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit. And he entered, and al-Jawniyyah had been brought in the house of Umaymah bint al-Numan ibn Sharahil, and with her a midwife of hers. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her he said: Give thyself to me. She said: And does a queen give herself to a commoner? She said: I seek refuge with Allah from thee. He said: Thou hast sought refuge with a Mighty One. Then he went out to us and said: O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two linen garments and join her to her family. He said: And other than Abu Ahmad said: A woman of Banu al-Jawn called Aminah."
"16159","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, he said: I heard Sahl say: Abu Usayd al-Saidi came and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wedding, and his wife was their servant that day, and she was the bride. He said: Do you know what she gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink? She soaked dates overnight in a stone cup."
"16160","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah said: And I heard it from Harun. He said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab al-Ansari narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Unays narrated to him that they mentioned, he and Umar ibn al-Khattab, one day charity. So Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he mentioned misappropriation of charity: He who misappropriates of it a camel or a sheep will be brought carrying it on the Day of Resurrection? Abdullah ibn Unays said: Yes."
